From aea8e54964d50ba720c260dbcc7868bee4bf7dcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Lasry <harrylasry@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:14:54 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] 3DO: the reset button and the OSD Reset start the game again

The core's CD drive forgets its disc on every console reset and waits for
Main to send one, as when a disc is loaded. After the OSD Reset or the
reset button, p3do_reset() only set a flag nobody read, so the BIOS found
an empty drive and showed its CD tray screen instead of starting the game
again: the disc had to be loaded again.

p3do_poll() now sends the info of the loaded disc again, with the console
held in reset, after p3do_reset(). It runs after the reset pulse of the
menu, which would clear the disc again. A disc loaded from the OSD sends
its info in its own reset and clears the flag.

Checked in the Verilator simulation of the 3DO core with this code: Doom,
OSD Reset at frame 1000: the drive reports the disc (status 0xC1) and
Doom starts again (the same pictures as its first start, 700 frames
later); before, the drive reported no disc (0x81) and the BIOS showed its
CD tray screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 support/3do/3do.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/support/3do/3do.cpp b/support/3do/3do.cpp
index 0ff001d..e7325cf 100644
--- a/support/3do/3do.cpp
+++ b/support/3do/3do.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,22 @@ void p3do_poll()
 	static unsigned long poll_timer = 0;
 	static uint8_t last_req = 255;
 
+	// A console reset (OSD Reset, reset button: p3do_reset) clears the disc of the core's drive, which waits
+	// for Main to send one. On a 3DO the disc stays in the drive: send it again with the console held in
+	// reset, so that the BIOS finds it and starts the game again. This runs after the reset pulse of the
+	// menu, which would clear the disc again.
+	if (need_reset)
+	{
+		static uint8_t info[2048];
+		need_reset = 0;
+		if (p3docdd.loaded && p3docdd.SendData && p3docdd.GetDiscInfo(info) > 0)
+		{
+			user_io_status_set("[0]", 1);
+			p3do_send_data(info, 2048, CD_INFO_IO_INDEX);
+			user_io_status_set("[0]", 0);
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (!poll_timer || CheckTimer(poll_timer))
 	{
 		poll_timer = GetTimer(0);
@@ -178,6 +194,7 @@ void p3do_set_image(int num, const char *filename)
 		}
 	}
 
+	need_reset = 0;	// the disc info was just sent with the console in reset
 	user_io_status_set("[0]", 0);
 }
 
